		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17169&amp;sid=dba1b842c7652a4157933cda01834eb1#17169"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Jan 08, 2004 5:51 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17169&amp;sid=dba1b842c7652a4157933cda01834eb1"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">For the record, I am indefinitely out of the game as a whole. I'm not sure if I have moved on or if it's just a hiatus at this point, but I have not logged on for some time. I have started a new position at work, and with that and other RL considerations I have realized I do not have near enough time to devote to this game at this point. It has little to do with the friends I have made here, in fact they're the reason my account is still active. If you feel so moved to remove me, understand I am not offended by this in the slightest, and I can always come looking you up when I am able to devote more attention to EQ. <img src="images/smiles/icon_wink.gif" alt="icon_wink.gif" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
Recruiting has never been our strong point. There are few who are willing to devote time to a completely rp guild. We are not known on Druzzil Ro, something I moved to correct, but the message never seemed to stick. I suggest a presence from an officer or even perhaps yourself, Arriik on druzzilro.com. Just my two cp...</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
