				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Hail Concordat.
<br />

<br />
I for one, had a very long absence from the game and felt poorly when I got back and saw how many had left.  I am, as you all have guessed a casual player who tries my best to RP when I can.  
<br />

<br />
Option 1.  Do nothing.  
<br />

<br />
This Option will keep us in no better a situation then we are now.  With out effort we will slowly fade into the shadows.
<br />

<br />
Option 2.  Recruit with no RP Focus.
<br />

<br />
I believe that this is an option with some limited possibilities.  Those that like to RP will be encouraged and those that don't will encouraged to have fun and we might convert some over.  Although, we will have to accept the fact that Evil will find it's way into our ranks.  There is a rash of SK and Necros out there, looking for ways to weaken the rightous.  Although, that makes for some of my best RP experiences of late in LDoN, proving the cuase of good and fairness.  (Helps when you get charmed and cut down the DE CLeric, DE SK and Gnome Necro.    <img src="images/smiles/icon_twisted.gif" alt="icon_twisted.gif" border="0" />  )  It is an option for a growth perspective.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Option 3  Merge with an Ally.
<br />

<br />
This also has some merit.  Although I do not personnaly know any of our allies, I believe there are many guilds that have our same views on the game and would be a good home for us.  
<br />

<br />
I have personal experience with the following guilds:  
<br />

<br />
Refiner's Fire -  Family Guild, with large population.
<br />

<br />
Unforgotten Path -  Small guild that has a Family First kinda mind.
<br />

<br />
I wish I could say more for other guilds, but alas, these are the people that I have the most experience with as of late.  I have made many friends in their ranks..
<br />

<br />

<br />
I would be willing to be an Officer and to help with recruiting if that is the goal we come to.  My intentions are to continue to carry my Cocordat Angelis Tag till it is ripped off.  (Bring a big axe when you come for it)
<br />

<br />
Till I see you all in game, 
<br />

<br />
Be well and may your Gods look over you
<br />

<br />

<br />
Ceowulf
<br />
Warrior of 50 Seasons.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
